181
00:15:22,433 --> 00:15:26,351
Your assignment has four questions. One: 2000 sports tops,

182
00:15:26,371 --> 00:15:31,239
an 80-centimetre neckline each, sewn in 605 with a 5.6-millimetre gauge,

183
00:15:31,259 --> 00:15:35,380
10 percent wastage and 5000-metre cones. Using today's model,

184
00:15:35,400 --> 00:15:39,386
find each thread's ratio, batch length and number of cones,

185
00:15:39,406 --> 00:15:42,577
and say which thread is most likely to run out.

186
00:15:42,977 --> 00:15:43,231
Two:

187
00:15:43,251 --> 00:15:48,232
the manual puts the spreader at its leftmost when the needle bar has come

188
00:15:48,252 --> 00:15:51,110
down 1.1 millimetres from top dead centre.

189
00:15:51,130 --> 00:15:55,564
Use the Chapter 3 formula to check that this is about 25 degrees,

190
00:15:55,584 --> 00:15:58,304
then find the angle for 2.0 millimetres.

191
00:15:58,324 --> 00:16:01,182
What happens if the spreader arrives late?

192
00:16:01,582 --> 00:16:04,380
Three: in Virtual lab 10-1,

193
00:16:04,400 --> 00:16:10,120
retard and then advance the looper timing by 5 degrees,

194
00:16:10,140 --> 00:16:16,173
and give the first criterion to fail, the fault you'd see,

195
00:16:16,193 --> 00:16:24,105
and the order of adjustment. Four, for discussion: on the same knit garment,

196
00:16:24,125 --> 00:16:32,037
why are hems usually 406, joining seams 605 or 607, and side seams overlock?

197
00:16:32,437 --> 00:16:34,545
Submit your working,

198
00:16:34,565 --> 00:16:41,143
the lab screenshots and the analysis on the WenQuest platform.

199
00:16:42,663 --> 00:16:46,371
There's also a ten-question quiz. For example,

200
00:16:46,391 --> 00:16:50,341
at standard settings the catch is at 214 degrees,

201
00:16:50,361 --> 00:16:55,527
with a rise of 3.36 millimetres. Retard the looper by 5 degrees:

202
00:16:55,547 --> 00:17:01,443
roughly how far has the needle risen at the catch, and is that a problem?

203
00:17:01,843 --> 00:17:09,129
Or, add a cover thread to 406 to get 602, with everything else the same.

204
00:17:09,149 --> 00:17:15,623
By what percentage does the thread per centimetre of seam go up?

205
00:17:16,023 --> 00:17:21,517
You get three attempts, and the explanations appear as soon as you submit.

206
00:17:23,037 --> 00:17:25,497
Three things to remember.

207
00:17:25,897 --> 00:17:29,827
One: a 401 stitch hinges on two moments: at the catch,

208
00:17:29,847 --> 00:17:35,606
the point enters the loop from behind the needle; when the next needle arrives,

209
00:17:35,626 --> 00:17:39,776
the point is in front and the needle enters the triangle.

210
00:17:40,176 --> 00:17:45,689
Two: the looper's swing and avoidance make a flat ellipse,

211
00:17:45,709 --> 00:17:51,796
and the timing window is only about minus 3.5 to plus 4 degrees.

212
00:17:52,196 --> 00:17:59,507
Three: count consumption thread by thread and stock cones the same way,

213
00:17:59,527 --> 00:18:02,089
with extra looper thread.

